# Normalise line endings in the repository, always.
#
# Without this, a Windows clone with the default `core.autocrlf=true` rewrites
# every checked-out file to CRLF. The app still runs, which is what makes it
# worth pinning: the damage is quiet. Diffs show every line as changed, so real
# review becomes impossible; a contributor's first pull request looks like they
# rewrote the file; and any check that matches source text exactly can start
# disagreeing with itself depending on who cloned it.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means: decide what is text, store it with LF, and check it
# out with LF on every platform. Windows editors have handled LF for years.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, byte for byte. Never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.wav binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.skill binary
